  "notes": "{垂|た}れる means for something to hang downward or for liquid to drip. It describes a passive, gravity-driven motion.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{垂|た}らす→垂らす：05339_tarasu⟧ (transitive, to let something hang/drip)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{垂|た}れて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ describes the resulting state of hanging down or dripping. Example: ⟦{枝|えだ}→枝：02181_eda⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{垂|た}れて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ (the branches are hanging down).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {頭|こうべ}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{垂|た}れる: to bow one's head (literary)\n- ⟦{汗|あせ}→汗：02173_ase⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{垂|た}れる: sweat drips\n- ⟦{枝|えだ}→枝：02181_eda⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{垂|た}れる: branches hang down\n- しだれ{桜|ざくら}: weeping cherry tree (from {垂|た}れる)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n⟦{実|みの}る→実る：00282_minoru⟧ほど{頭|こうべ}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{垂|た}れる⟦{稲穂|いなほ}→稲穂：10175_inaho⟧⟦か→か：09473_ka⟧な — The more accomplished one becomes, the more humble one should be. A well-known proverb comparing the bowing rice stalk to humility.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{垂|た}らす→垂らす：05339_tarasu⟧: to let hang, to drip (transitive)\n- ⟦{下|さ}がる→下がる：01188_sagaru⟧: to go down, to hang (more general)",
